From: hashtagbasit
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: sm8650: PCIe sleep floor at CX retention

With no PCIe suspend OPP at all, a Pocket FIT never woke from s2idle (it had
to be restarted), so the system needs PCIe's DDR vote in the sleep set to
resume. The suspend OPP it got before also required CX at low_svs, and a CX
level above retention for the whole sleep rules out CX collapse.

Keep the floor's DDR vote and ask only for CX retention, the lowest level,
which CX can still sleep at.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
@@ -3761,6 +3761,17 @@
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1969000 1>;
 					opp-level = <3>;
 				};
+
+				/*
+				 * Sleep floor (s2idle): DDR stays voted so the system can
+				 * resume, CX only at retention so it can still collapse.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_ret>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 			};
 
 			pcieport0: pcie@0 {
